  {
    "_meta": {
      "description": "Candidate axis tick-mark pixel-position ground truth for verified_pairs, generated by two independent vision-LLM judges (Claude Opus 5 and Claude Fable 5), NOT human-verified. See docs/design/benchmark-architecture.md and https://github.com/t29mato/real-chart-bench/issues/5 for context and known caveats (multi-panel/inset ambiguity across several verified_pairs images).",
      "generated_at": "2026-08-30",
      "method": "Each of 42 verified_pairs images was shown independently to claude-opus-5 and claude-fable-5, asked to read the smallest/largest tick label on each axis and the pixel coordinate of that tick, then cross-checked its own answer via pixel-level dark-line/tick profiling (not just a single vision read). Agreement across the two independent models: 42/42 identical tick label values; pixel-position disagreement averaged 0.030% and maxed 0.22% of the relevant image dimension (~1-3px). This is a strong *consistency* signal, not proof of correctness -- a 10-image subset was also spot-checked visually by overlaying both models' picks on the source image.",
      "status_values": {
        "llm_candidate": "Both models agree on tick labels; pixel positions are the mean of the two models' estimates. Not yet human-verified.",
        "owner_reviewed": "The repo owner visually spot-checked this entry's overlay (both models' picks rendered on the source image) and confirmed it looks correct. Still LLM-generated, not independently re-measured by a human."
      },
      "known_caveats": [
        "crops/17044/fig2a.png: main-plot x-axis tick labels are cropped out of the image; the 0-300 range was inferred from the co-located fig2b (identical frame) and the inset's shared temperature axis, not read directly.",
        "crops/21682/fig4a.png and fig4b.png: each crop shows a sliver of the neighboring panel's heading letter bleeding in at the edge ('b' in fig4a, 'c' in fig4b) -- this is just crop-boundary bleed from the source figure's per-panel heading placement, not a data/metadata error; fig4b.png's actual content matches the registry's 'panel b' evidence.",
        "images/47998/p08_embedded_7.jpg: 5-panel figure; panel (a) has no numeric y-axis tick labels (Intensity a.u.) so panel (b) was used instead.",
        "crops/5904/corrected_fig5.png: the source figure is rotated 90 degrees; pixel coordinates are reported in image-pixel orientation (see this entry's notes), not the plot's own x/y orientation.",
        "Images without an explicit panel note but with more than one panel in frame (images/5166, images/18759, images/17037) had panel (a) selected by default since no panel was specified to the judges.",
        "images/17037, images/47998: the initial judging pass (before per-panel labels were cross-checked against registry.json) picked the wrong panel for these two composite images (registry.json specifies panel 'd' and 'c' respectively, but panel 'a' and 'b' were judged instead). Fixed by re-cropping to the correct single panel and re-judging; see each entry's notes.",
        "crops/17044/fig2a.png: excluded from owner_reviewed pending a decision on how to handle images whose axis is only recoverable via a sibling panel (see https://github.com/t29mato/real-chart-bench/issues/5)."
      ],
